namtor (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the namtor-kde binary package: the project consolidated on a
    single desktop-neutral GTK4/libadwaita UI, so the Plasma 6 KCM and
    its cmake/qt6-base-dev/libkf6*-dev build dependencies are gone.
  * namtor-gnome now declares Replaces/Breaks: namtor-kde. This is an
    upgrade-blocker fix, not tidiness: namtor-kde declared
    Depends: namtor (= <version>), so a leftover install of it would
    hold apt back from upgrading the core package.
  * namtor-gnome Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-2).

 -- Nam-tor Project <namtor@example.invalid>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

namtor (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split into namtor (core), namtor-gnome, namtor-kde binary packages.
  * Core: daemon, worker, CLI, PAM module, systemd units, sysusers,
    tmpfiles, D-Bus, polkit, manifests, bundled models + licence
    notices, lifecycle helper, SBOM. No GTK/Qt runtime deps.
  * namtor-gnome: GTK4/libadwaita wizard; Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-1).
  * namtor-kde: Plasma 6 KCM (Kirigami/Qt6); Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-1).
  * PAM module at Debian multiarch path
    (/usr/lib/<triplet>/security/pam_namtor.so).
  * PAM remains OFF by default; remove keeps state, purge cleans all.
  * Models bundled from deterministic signed archive (no network fetch).

 -- Nam-tor Project <namtor@example.invalid>  Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
